msgid "Content"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/facilitator.rst:303
msgid "``GET /x402/supply``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/facilitator.rst:304
msgid ""
"The latest epoch, the signed chain, its head, and the witnesses that have"
" pinned it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/facilitator.rst:306
msgid "``GET /x402/issuance``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/facilitator.rst:307
msgid "The issuance chain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/facilitator.rst:308
msgid "``GET /x402/issuance/head``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/facilitator.rst:309
msgid "The current head of the chain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/facilitator.rst:310
msgid "``GET /x402/witnesses``, ``POST /x402/witness``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/facilitator.rst:311
msgid ""
"The statements peers and others have made about the head, and the route "
"to submit one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/facilitator.rst:313
#, python-brace-format
msgid "``GET /agents/{aid}/liability-proof``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/facilitator.rst:314
msgid "The proof that an account's balance is part of an epoch's total."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/facilitator.rst:316
msgid ""
"On a node, ``anet audit-hub`` checks the chain and the node's own proof; "
"see :ref:`reference-cli`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/facilitator.rst:319
msgid "The operator reads the same figures with ``anet-hub supply``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/facilitator.rst:332
msgid ""
"``latest_epoch`` lists the sequence number, the first and last day, the "
"outstanding amount and the Merkle root of the latest published epoch, or "
"the word ``none``. ``due`` lines are what this hub owes a peer, and "
"``owed`` lines what a peer owes this hub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/facilitator.rst:341
msgid "Redemption"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/facilitator.rst:343
msgid ""
"An account holder returns credit to the hub with ``anet redeem``. The "
"credit leaves circulation and the hub signs a receipt. What the credit is"
" exchanged for outside the hub is an agreement between operator and "
"account holder; the ``reference`` the holder attached to the request is "
"the identifier to use. The operator lists the redemptions to be handled:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/facilitator.rst:355
msgid ""
"Each line holds the time, the AID, the amount, the quoted reference and "
"the authorization id. With ``--json`` the same list is printed with the "
"count, the sum and ``window_days``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/facilitator.rst:361
msgid "Between hubs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/facilitator.rst:363
msgid ""
"Settlements for a payee on another hub make this hub owe the ledger hub "
"and the other way round. ``anet-hub due`` and ``anet-hub clear`` reduce "
"these obligations (see :ref:`ops-federation`). The payment of real value "
"that accompanies a clearing is outside the hub."
msgstr ""

